2026-08-31T00:02:50Z (RFD66606-2143) 'What this RFD does not cover
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2143  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-31T00:02:51Z (RFD66606-2143) '- **Cross-region.** R2 IA in one region is one regional outage away
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2143  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-31T00:02:52Z (RFD66606-2143) '  from no backup at all. A second R2 region is a later change.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2143  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-31T00:02:53Z (RFD66606-2143) '- **Backup encryption at rest.** FDB does not encrypt backup
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2143  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-31T00:02:54Z (RFD66606-2143) '  payloads. If R2 is compromised, the attacker has the database.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2143  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-31T00:02:55Z (RFD66606-2143) '  `fdbbackup --encryption-key-file` is the fix; it needs its own
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2143  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-31T00:02:56Z (RFD66606-2143) '  key management story.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2143  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-31T00:02:57Z (RFD66606-2143) '- **PITR window.** The `dr` tag keeps 10-day snapshots
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2143  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-31T00:02:58Z (RFD66606-2143) '  (`Snapshot interval is 864000 seconds`), at IA rates.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2143  1 LINE
 Text:Written

